luce-usd is a rewrite in Luce of parts of OpenUSD (Universal Scene
Description), and is a derivative work of OpenUSD. It follows OpenUSD's
data model, file formats and composition algorithms, and ports their
structure from the C++ sources of release v26.08.

OpenUSD is available at https://github.com/PixarAnimationStudios/OpenUSD
and is licensed under the Tomorrow Open Source Technology License 1.0,
included in licenses/OPENUSD-TOST-1.0.txt. That license is the Apache
License 2.0 with a different Section 6 ("Trademarks"): it grants no
permission to use Pixar's trade names, trademarks or product names.

